I am reposting this after deleting the original (along with Robin and And's 
messages that quoted the original).  I removed them from the Yahoogroups 
archives, even though it appears that their archives partially hide email 
addresses to protect against this very thing.  Someone complained about a 
sudden increase in spam, and opined that the list of email addressed 
appearing on the list was responsible.  (My apologies to that person and 
any others similarly afflicted).  Someone subscribed to one of these lists 
is apparently harvesting email addresses for spam purposes, so we'll have 
to be more careful.



